  "articleBody": "It's a common question, and the answer isn't always a simple 'yes' or 'no' – it depends on several factors, but the short version is: yes, absolutely. In California, if your blood alcohol content (BAC) is 0.08% or higher, you can be arrested for DUI. For commercial drivers, it's even lower at 0.04%, and for drivers under 21, any detectable alcohol can lead to an arrest. Even if your BAC is below 0.08%, you can still be arrested if an officer believes your driving is impaired by alcohol or drugs. This is often referred to as 'driving under the influence.' Things like swerving, slow reaction times, or failing field sobriety tests can all contribute to an officer's assessment. It's a serious charge, with potential consequences far beyond just a fine, including license suspension and even jail time. If you find yourself in this situation, whether it's in El Cajon, Oceanside, or anywhere in San Diego County, understanding your rights and having an experienced criminal defense lawyer on your side, like Angelo J. Reyes, is crucial. They can help navigate the complexities of DUI defense and work to protect your future.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
